<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Saudi Arabia</h1><p class="st-meta">1932 CE – present · capital Riyadh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Al Saud kingdom covering most of the Arabian Peninsula, guardian of Mecca and Medina and one of the world's largest oil producers.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Abd al-Aziz ibn Saud</a> unified the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hejaz-and-nejd">Kingdom of Hejaz and Nejd</a> as the Kingdom of Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> on 23 September 1932, completing three decades of conquest begun with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-nejd-and-hasa">Emirate of Nejd and Hasa</a>. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/idrisid-emirate-of-asir">Idrisid Emirate of Asir</a> was absorbed by 1934, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-taif">Treaty of Ta'if</a> with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-yemen">Yemen</a> fixed the southern border.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> is an absolute monarchy whose kings rule with the support of the Wahhabi religious establishment. Oil found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dammam">Dammam</a> in 1938 and developed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saudi-aramco">Aramco</a> funded a vast state. King Faisal used the 1973 oil embargo as a political weapon. The 1979 seizure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masjid-al-haram">Grand Mosque</a> led to stricter religious policies, and the kingdom hosted coalition forces in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-war">Gulf War</a> of 1990-1991.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Succession has passed among the sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Abd al-Aziz</a>. Under King Salman, from 2015, Crown Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammed-bin-salman">Mohammed bin Salman</a> launched the Vision 2030 programme to diversify the economy and relaxed some social restrictions, while concentrating power further.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/saudi-arabia.jpg" alt="Saudi Arabia" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: The Shura Council · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Saudi_Arabia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1932 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Riyadh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abd al-Aziz ibn Saud, Faisal bin Abdulaziz, Salman bin Abdulaziz</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Saudi Arabia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1979&amp;focus=saudi-arabia" aria-label="Saudi Arabia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5921 1271 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Saudi Arabia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6241 1527L6241 1527M6241 1527L6159 1797"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6241 1527h0M6159 1797h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6241 1527h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6241 1527h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Riyadh. <a href="/atlas?year=1979&amp;focus=saudi-arabia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
